{"_v":1,"id":"the-woman-in-white-2005","bd":{"positive":0,"mixed":1,"negative":1},"rv":[{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":44,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2005/11/18/theater/reviews/the-woman-in-white-a-musical-shrouded-in-gloom.html","d":"2005-11-18","q":"This expensive import from London, based on Wilkie Collins's 1860 novel, is a musical that seems to have been conceived in a perpetual fog bank. Even when the stage is brightly lighted, you feel as if you're peering through thick gauze at characters who never quite come into focus."},{"cn":"Matthew Murray","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":59,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.talkinbroadway.com/world/WomanInWhite.html","d":"2005-11-27","q":"Practically everyone else, unfortunately including the ever-reliable Walter Charles as Laura and Marian's crotchety uncle, tends to fade into the background."}],"au":{"score":53,"designation":"Loathing","sources":{"mz":{"s":53,"c":12,"sr":2.6}}},"ta":"210 W 46th St, New York, NY 10036","pd":"2005-10-28","ca":[{"n":"Michael Ball","r":"Count Fosco"},{"n":"Ron Bohmer","r":"Sir Percival Glyde"},{"n":"Adam Brazier","r":"Walter Hartright"},{"n":"Walter Charles","r":"Mr. Fairlie"},{"n":"Angela Christian","r":"Anne Catherick"},{"n":"Maria Friedman","r":"Marian Halcombe"},{"n":"Jill Paice","r":"Laura Fairlie"},{"n":"Richard Todd Adams","r":"Con Man"},{"n":"Justis Bolding","r":"Corn Dolly Girl"},{"n":"John Dewar","r":"Mr. Fairlie's Servant"},{"n":"Patty Goble","r":"Nurse"},{"n":"Norman Large","r":"Signal Man"}]}